WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.715
Windows, Linux, and macOS can all support local inference.

00:00:03.715 --> 00:00:08.132
The practical choice depends on hardware support, operator skill, application needs,

00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:12.148
security controls, automation, and the ability to maintain the environment.

00:00:12.148 --> 00:00:15.763
NVIDIA acceleration commonly relies on CUDA-compatible drivers and runtimes.

00:00:15.763 --> 00:00:21.787
AMD support may use ROCm or other compatible paths depending on hardware and operating system.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:25.803
Vulkan can provide a cross-platform acceleration option for supported runtimes.

00:00:25.803 --> 00:00:28.615
Apple Silicon uses Metal and unified memory,

00:00:28.615 --> 00:00:32.631
allowing CPU and GPU components to share a memory pool.

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:36.647
Available capacity, bandwidth, thermals, and model support still set limits.

00:00:36.647 --> 00:00:40.262
Unified memory should not be treated as unlimited VRAM.

00:00:40.262 --> 00:00:45.483
Driver and runtime versions must align with the hardware, operating system, inference software,

00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:46.286
and libraries.

00:00:46.286 --> 00:00:51.105
A powerful GPU can perform poorly or fail to load a model

00:00:51.105 --> 00:00:54.318
when the acceleration stack is unsupported or inconsistent.

00:00:54.318 --> 00:00:57.129
Stability matters more than chasing every update.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:01.949
Maintain a known working configuration, record versions, review release changes, test upgrades,

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:03.555
and preserve rollback options.

00:01:03.555 --> 00:01:07.170
Security updates and unsupported dependencies still need timely attention.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.383
The software environment is part of capacity planning.

00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:13.997
Background applications, display usage, antivirus or security scanning, containers,

00:01:13.997 --> 00:01:18.415
virtual machines, and multiple runtimes can consume memory and complicate troubleshooting.

00:01:18.415 --> 00:01:19.620
Standardize before tuning.
